# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# ⚠️ THIS IS THE TEMPLATE. `bin/init` copies it to `piezas.tsv` on install.
#    It ships WITH the engine's rows already filled in — unlike cuentas.tsv,
#    this file cannot be born empty: without the engine rows, check-structure
#    has nothing to verify and goes silent about every piece that disappears.
#
# ⭐ KEEP IT IN SYNC WITH THE LIVE FILE. Every piece added to the engine needs
#    its row here too, or a fresh clone installs a table that does not describe
#    what it actually received — and the gap is silent, which is the worst kind.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# piezas.tsv — the single source of truth for WHERE each key piece lives.
# Read by bin/check-structure; verified by bin/test-f0-f6.
#
# ⭐ Moving a piece costs ONE line here. Do not hardcode a location in prose —
#    point at this table. A piece written but not declared here is a piece that
#    check-structure goes SILENT about when it disappears.
#
# Format (TAB-separated):  pieza <TAB> ruta <TAB> governance <TAB> clase <TAB> que_es
#
#   governance — WHO decides over this piece (authority, never a person's name):
#     engine   the engine governs it · universal · travels identical to every clone
#     owner    whoever installs the instance governs it · their criterion · NEVER a name
#     shared   the engine defines the FORM, the owner fills the CONTENT
#
#   clase — HOW the piece is born:
#     canonical  written by hand · the source of truth
#     generated  produced by a script (bin/generate-*)
#     fossil     historical · kept for reference · not live
#
# ⛔ governance answers a DIFFERENT question than clase. Do not merge them.
# ⛔ No instance data in any row: no owner name, no real repo/project name in que_es.
#    A person's name was never a governance value — it was a leak. The value is
#    the ROLE ("owner"), never who currently holds it.
#
# ⭐ HOW TO TELL engine FROM owner — the test that settles it:
#    ask "would a different installation edit this file?"  No  → engine.
#    A file the owner READS but never rewrites is engine (base-rules.md, the
#    four architects): doctrine ships identical, and mislabelling it as owner
#    would hide it from any check that verifies engine files carry no instance
#    data. The frontier in mente.config.yml is the authority; this column must
#    agree with it.
#
# ⚠️ THE `owner` ROWS DO NOT EXIST ON A FRESH CLONE. check-structure reports
#    them red until you write each one. ⭐ That red is your install checklist,
#    not a fault — a check that turned green there would be lying.
#
# ⬜ ADD YOUR OWN PIECES at the end, under their own section comment. A piece
#    of yours that is not declared here is a piece the structure check cannot
#    protect: the day it disappears, nothing says so.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
pieza	ruta	governance	clase	que_es
